NAME
       host - look up names and addresses in DNS

SYNOPSIS
       host [-t TYPE] [-v] NAME [SERVER]

DESCRIPTION
       host asks a DNS server for the address of a host name, or for the name
       of an address (a reverse lookup). It uses the servers listed in
       /etc/resolv.conf unless a SERVER is given. Unlike getent hosts, host
       asks DNS only and never reads /etc/hosts, so it shows whether the DNS
       settings themselves work.

       host comes in the bind-utils package (with dig and nslookup), which is
       not installed on a minimal RHEL 9 system: dnf install bind-utils.

OPTIONS
       -t TYPE
              The record type to ask for: A, AAAA, MX, PTR, NS and so on.

       -v     Verbose: print the whole answer, in the style of dig.

EXIT STATUS
       0 when the name was found, 1 when it was not.

EXAMPLES
              $ host utility.lab.example.com
              utility.lab.example.com has address 192.168.50.254

              $ host 192.168.50.254
              254.50.168.192.in-addr.arpa domain name pointer utility.lab.example.com.

SEE ALSO
       dig(1), nslookup(1), getent(1), resolv.conf(5)
